SETTINGS toggle interactions: clicking the SKY checkbox toggles it and re-renders bit-identically.

Clicking a widget inside the SETTINGS screen SIGSEGV'd in the display-list element ACTIVATE handler
FUN_0000_6af0 at `*(int*)(param_2+6)` (fault-addr 0x3bae).  Reconstructing the click->toggle->re-paint
path fixed three asm-verified defects (vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin); the SKY checkbox now toggles its
state, updates the status line, and re-paints its indicator OFF -- byte-identical to the DOSBox
reference (flow settings-sky).

1. FUN_0000_6af0 (asm 0x6af0..0x6b26) -- the element ACTIVATE method, dispatched by the hit-test
   fist_hit1eb4 via `[element+0x4660]` (asm 0x1f8c: `mov ds:0x3e08,bx; mov di,[bx]; call [di+0x4660]`)
   with AX=event flags, BX=element (a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET), BP=walk-base (DGROUP offset).  The dispatch
   already threads (flags, elem, base) (patch 142), but 6af0 used elem/base as RAW HOST POINTERS
   (base-loss).  Rebase to g_mem+0x1c000; thread the CF; call the "pressed" flash via [DGROUP:0x626]
   with the widget rect (bx=elem+4).

2. FUN_0000_6b27 (asm 0x6b27: `call WORD PTR cs:[bx+0x6b2d]`) -- the near-handler dispatch (id ->
   handler: 6bb1=SKY, 6b60/6be7/6c02/6c1d=other checkboxes, 6bcc/6bd5/6bde=DETAIL radios).  Ghidra
   deref'd `param_1+0x6b2d` as a host address; rebase to the CS=0 image base g_mem+(uint16)(param_1+
   0x6b2d).

3. TWO store-width bugs (the patch 104/134 class), exposed for the first time by reaching the toggle:
   - The SKY checkbox STATE flag 0x8b46 (DAT_2000_4b46) is a BYTE (asm `xor byte`/`cmp byte`) but was
     typed WORD -> the SKY handler 6bb1's word XOR/compare pulled in the adjacent DETAIL byte 0x8b47
     (=0x04): word 0x0401->0x0400, so the state byte 0x8b46=0 (correct) yet word!=0 -> the wrong status
     string ("SKY ENABLED") + kept the indicator lit.  Retype to BYTE (only 6bb1 uses this macro).
   - The SKY widget DIRTY flag 0x8ba9 (DAT_2000_4ba9) is a BYTE (asm `mov byte,3`) but was typed WORD
     -> `= 3` wrote 0x0003 as a word, clobbering the adjacent renderer-index byte 0x8baa (0x10->0) so
     the dirty-walk 209e re-paint dispatched the WRONG renderer (6cb6 instead of 6ce5=SKY) -> the
     indicator never re-rendered OFF.  Retype to BYTE (this macro is only ever written `= 3`).

The "pressed" flash (6af0's [DGROUP:0x626] call = MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_1290, the box-outline XOR draw) is
kept at its current pristine state (a stub -> its cursor-hide 2d6d): 1290's box-outline body is dropped
by Ghidra ("does not return"), and its sibling [0x626] box-wrapper callers 64a4/aa4e (dialog box draws
on the list-dialog paint paths, e.g. BATTLES) carry pre-existing DROPPED element args -- reconstructing
1290 to actually draw surfaces those as garbage-rect corruption (a flake in the battles/campaigns
flows).  The flash is a 1-frame XOR transient that is repainted before the frame settles (verified: the
DOSBox settled reference shows no flash), so the box-outline draw is absent from every verified frame;
reconstructing 1290 + threading the 64a4/aa4e box-wrapper element args is a separate deferred deliverable.

Result: byte-identical to the DOSBox reference (flow settings-sky, AE=0 native + wasm, native<->wasm
0-diff, deterministic).  Reached only by clicking inside SETTINGS -> the 19 prior flows are
behaviour-neutral (6af0/6b27 are widget-click-only; 4b46 is read only by 6bb1; 4ba9 is only ever
written =3; 1290 is untouched -> battles/campaigns unaffected).

